WEBVTT

1
00:01:04,512 --> 00:01:06,238
Pull over the van!

2
00:01:09,586 --> 00:01:10,691
I'm sorry.

3
00:01:10,725 --> 00:01:11,692
Okay, guys.

4
00:01:12,520 --> 00:01:15,282
I understand what
you're feeling.

5
00:01:15,661 --> 00:01:18,457
We don't need to go
where we're going, okay?

6
00:01:18,492 --> 00:01:21,184
Just pull the van
over and we'll talk.

7
00:01:21,219 --> 00:01:23,152
<i>It feels so good right now.</i>

8
00:01:37,442 --> 00:01:39,133
I just need you to listen, okay?

9
00:01:39,168 --> 00:01:41,653
I just need you to fucking
listen to me! I...!

10
00:01:43,896 --> 00:01:45,208
I'm so sorry.

11
00:01:56,288 --> 00:01:57,910
I don't want to go see the boy!

12
00:01:57,945 --> 00:01:59,636
I don't want to see
the fucking boy!

13
00:01:59,671 --> 00:02:01,535
I don't want to see the boy!

14
00:02:01,569 --> 00:02:03,778
Not the boy!
Not the boy!

15
00:02:03,813 --> 00:02:05,228
Not the boy!

16
00:02:05,263 --> 00:02:06,298
Not the boy!

17
00:02:06,333 --> 00:02:07,161
Not the--

18
00:02:22,625 --> 00:02:25,317
<i>My name is Ellen Hershbergen</i>

19
00:02:25,352 --> 00:02:27,526
<i>and I will tell you
all that happened</i>

20
00:02:27,561 --> 00:02:29,666
<i>in hopes that
it will never happen again.</i>

21
00:02:31,772 --> 00:02:33,981
<i>My mother died in February.</i>

22
00:02:34,015 --> 00:02:35,879
<i>She had been
battling Alzheimer's.</i>

23
00:02:37,916 --> 00:02:40,574
<i>I had been all kinds
of things before that.</i>

24
00:02:41,575 --> 00:02:44,336
<i>A modestly successful
fashion designer.</i>

25
00:02:44,371 --> 00:02:47,408
<i>The author of
a children's book about peas.</i>

26
00:02:48,237 --> 00:02:50,170
<i>Then I became a caretaker.</i>

27
00:02:50,860 --> 00:02:53,690
<i>Now, I wasn't even that.</i>

28
00:02:56,693 --> 00:03:01,974
<i>So all I could do is reinvent
myself and start over.</i>

29
00:03:02,009 --> 00:03:02,975
Morning.

30
00:03:04,045 --> 00:03:05,012
I'm father John Dore.

31
00:03:05,978 --> 00:03:08,222
- Nice to meet you.
- Lovely to meet you, too.

32
00:03:08,843 --> 00:03:10,328
Your call was a godsend.

33
00:03:10,362 --> 00:03:11,812
I've been needing a hand,

34
00:03:11,846 --> 00:03:13,745
but I don't have
the budget to hire

35
00:03:13,779 --> 00:03:14,780
someone full time.

36
00:03:14,815 --> 00:03:17,369
I used to volunteer at
my church in Buffalo,

37
00:03:17,404 --> 00:03:19,682
so I thought it might help me
find my footing here.

38
00:03:19,716 --> 00:03:22,340
And why Pontiac?
How did we get so lucky?

39
00:03:22,374 --> 00:03:24,549
Uh, more chance than luck.

40
00:03:24,963 --> 00:03:26,861
I had this weird feeling

41
00:03:27,690 --> 00:03:30,348
I could fit here,
be myself again.

42
00:03:32,764 --> 00:03:36,354
You know, we could pull
together a yard sale,

43
00:03:36,388 --> 00:03:38,563
raise some money,
fix the pews.

44
00:03:38,597 --> 00:03:39,978
I'm actually pretty good
at that.

45
00:03:40,634 --> 00:03:41,738
Yes.

46
00:03:42,843 --> 00:03:43,947
All right.
It's worth a shot.

47
00:03:43,982 --> 00:03:44,948
Yes.

48
00:03:53,647 --> 00:03:55,511
Donna. Hi.

49
00:03:55,545 --> 00:03:58,755
<i>Ellen, how's the new town
treating you?</i>

50
00:03:58,790 --> 00:04:00,447
Oh, uh.

51
00:04:00,481 --> 00:04:01,413
It's good.

52
00:04:01,448 --> 00:04:04,899
Quiet. Not tripping
over boxes anymore.

53
00:04:04,934 --> 00:04:05,900
It suits me.

54
00:04:05,935 --> 00:04:08,972
<i>I'm glad.
Buffalo will miss you.</i>

55
00:04:09,007 --> 00:04:10,664
<i>You needed a new start.</i>

56
00:04:10,698 --> 00:04:13,667
Yeah. Thanks, Donna.
I really did.

57
00:04:13,701 --> 00:04:16,532
<i>Hey, do you remember
our Cousin Winthrop?</i>

58
00:04:16,566 --> 00:04:18,016
Babysat for him every Thursday.

59
00:04:18,050 --> 00:04:19,466
Ate his weight in spaghetti.

60
00:04:19,500 --> 00:04:20,570
Of course
I remember him.

61
00:04:20,605 --> 00:04:22,676
<i>He's been staying
with us for a while</i>

62
00:04:22,710 --> 00:04:25,299
<i>but Dan wants him gone.</i>

63
00:04:25,334 --> 00:04:26,749
<i>Not enough space
in the house.</i>

64
00:04:26,783 --> 00:04:28,060
Right.

65
00:04:28,095 --> 00:04:30,546
<i>Good news is he's got
a job at a sheet metal plant</i>

66
00:04:30,580 --> 00:04:32,513
<i>not too far
from Pontiac, actually.</i>

67
00:04:32,548 --> 00:04:34,101
<i>Starts in the spring--</i>

68
00:04:34,135 --> 00:04:37,691
You don't even have to finish.
I would be happy to have him.

69
00:04:37,725 --> 00:04:40,659
<i>Really? That would be amazing.</i>

70
00:04:40,694 --> 00:04:41,867
Of course.

71
00:04:41,902 --> 00:04:43,455
<i>He's been bouncing
around family for years.</i>

72
00:04:43,490 --> 00:04:46,355
<i>Like a ball with no air in it.</i>

73
00:04:46,389 --> 00:04:49,703
<i>Just know Winthrop
is a little different.</i>

74
00:04:49,737 --> 00:04:51,532
<i>He has some PTSD stuff</i>

75
00:04:51,567 --> 00:04:53,707
<i>from his time in the army.</i>

76
00:04:53,741 --> 00:04:55,398
<i>But he's a good guy.</i>

77
00:04:56,123 --> 00:04:58,815
All right,
well, we'll figure it out.

78
00:04:58,850 --> 00:05:01,473
I think it might do me some
good to have someone around.

79
00:05:02,440 --> 00:05:04,925
<i>Thank you, Ellen.
Okay, bye.</i>

80
00:05:04,959 --> 00:05:06,927
All right. Bye, Donna.

81
00:05:35,576 --> 00:05:36,577
Winthrop?

82
00:05:40,063 --> 00:05:41,375
Cousin Helen?

83
00:05:42,859 --> 00:05:44,551
It's been a long time.

84
00:05:44,585 --> 00:05:46,380
Only about 30 years.

85
00:05:50,971 --> 00:05:52,110
Is that all you have?

86
00:05:52,869 --> 00:05:53,939
That's all I need.

87
00:05:55,838 --> 00:05:56,977
All right.

88
00:05:58,012 --> 00:06:00,152
I appreciate you taking me in
for a while.

89
00:06:03,224 --> 00:06:04,778
Thank you.

90
00:06:04,812 --> 00:06:05,917
Glad for the company.

91
00:06:06,745 --> 00:06:08,126
It's really good to see you.

92
00:06:20,863 --> 00:06:21,864
This is it.

93
00:06:23,866 --> 00:06:25,385
Let me show you your room.

94
00:06:39,537 --> 00:06:40,538
You like it?

95
00:06:43,195 --> 00:06:44,818
Look. That's us.

96
00:06:55,138 --> 00:06:56,105
Thank you.

97
00:07:02,663 --> 00:07:03,664
Okay.

98
00:07:04,147 --> 00:07:06,874
I had never seen
anyone inhale

99
00:07:06,909 --> 00:07:08,531
spaghetti and meatballs
like you did.

100
00:07:09,083 --> 00:07:10,499
You remember?

101
00:07:10,533 --> 00:07:11,534
It was almost scary.

102
00:07:12,155 --> 00:07:13,191
I still do.

103
00:07:14,675 --> 00:07:16,988
I was sorry to hear
about your mom.

104
00:07:17,022 --> 00:07:17,920
Mm.

105
00:07:19,680 --> 00:07:20,854
Thanks.

106
00:07:21,164 --> 00:07:24,892
I remember her always
laughing, telling jokes.

107
00:07:27,688 --> 00:07:28,689
Mm.

108
00:07:29,276 --> 00:07:31,692
She was a good cook,
like you.

109
00:07:31,727 --> 00:07:33,038
Mm. Thanks.

110
00:07:33,798 --> 00:07:35,040
She was.

111
00:07:35,558 --> 00:07:37,974
She had a laugh that
could fill the whole house.

112
00:07:41,046 --> 00:07:44,498
Then your parents...
nothing about that was fair.

113
00:07:54,059 --> 00:07:55,198
Let's get you some more.

114
00:08:15,736 --> 00:08:17,600
Would it be okay
if I take a bath?

115
00:08:18,256 --> 00:08:19,775
Mm. Of course.

116
00:08:38,241 --> 00:08:39,588
Oh!

117
00:09:41,063 --> 00:09:42,029
Winthrop?

118
00:10:21,828 --> 00:10:23,105
Winthrop?

119
00:10:50,063 --> 00:10:51,202
Hm.

120
00:10:53,307 --> 00:10:55,447
I don't believe I ever met
your uncle Ray.

121
00:10:55,482 --> 00:10:57,173
Your father's
younger brother, right?

122
00:11:02,938 --> 00:11:05,216
I'm sorry.
I don't want to talk about that.

123
00:11:06,942 --> 00:11:07,908
Sure.

124
00:11:13,189 --> 00:11:17,918
I find it hard to reckon what
people do to one another.

125
00:11:20,231 --> 00:11:23,165
No, you don't have to think
about any of that here.

126
00:11:33,140 --> 00:11:35,073
Something's on your mind.

127
00:11:35,798 --> 00:11:37,041
Wanna share?

128
00:11:38,180 --> 00:11:40,492
It's my cousin... Winthrop.

129
00:11:41,183 --> 00:11:42,736
He's staying with me, and...

130
00:11:44,462 --> 00:11:48,811
I'm not sorry I took him in,
but he's been through a lot.

131
00:11:49,432 --> 00:11:51,055
Fought in Afghanistan.

132
00:11:51,365 --> 00:11:52,470
He doesn't sleep.

133
00:11:52,504 --> 00:11:53,782
Walks all night.

134
00:11:55,128 --> 00:11:57,717
Locks himself in the bathroom
for hours.

135
00:11:58,200 --> 00:11:59,995
Eye contact is a struggle.

136
00:12:01,272 --> 00:12:03,792
And I just keep wondering if
he should be with someone

137
00:12:03,826 --> 00:12:07,036
who can handle real PTSD.

138
00:12:07,899 --> 00:12:11,834
Someone who doesn't just sit
outside the bathroom door

139
00:12:11,869 --> 00:12:13,111
hoping he'll come out.

140
00:12:14,388 --> 00:12:16,528
Sometimes that's enough.

141
00:12:16,563 --> 00:12:18,427
Someone waiting
outside the door.

142
00:12:18,979 --> 00:12:20,049
Huh?

143
00:12:21,085 --> 00:12:23,363
That's what
I told myself with my mom.

144
00:12:24,882 --> 00:12:27,229
I stayed in case...

145
00:12:29,887 --> 00:12:33,062
she came back out
just for a minute.

146
00:12:33,097 --> 00:12:34,339
She never did.

147
00:12:35,478 --> 00:12:37,895
I can't let
that happen to Winthrop.

148
00:12:38,309 --> 00:12:41,277
I failed him once,
and I won't do it again.

149
00:12:42,106 --> 00:12:43,314
Ellen...

150
00:12:44,004 --> 00:12:47,076
you did more for her than
most people ever get.

151
00:12:48,008 --> 00:12:49,941
Now you're doing the same
for Winthrop.

152
00:13:14,345 --> 00:13:15,346
Oh.

153
00:13:15,933 --> 00:13:17,797
I'm sorry, I didn't hear
you pull up.

154
00:13:18,590 --> 00:13:19,833
Vahna.

155
00:13:19,868 --> 00:13:21,283
Oh, hi.
I am... I am Ellen.

156
00:13:21,317 --> 00:13:23,112
Oh, wow.

157
00:13:23,147 --> 00:13:26,288
You had a lot of work done here
in such a short amount of time.

158
00:13:26,322 --> 00:13:28,152
Well, it's good to have someone
helping you.

159
00:13:28,186 --> 00:13:29,118
It rains a lot here,

160
00:13:29,153 --> 00:13:32,501
so everything just gets
really overgrown.

161
00:13:32,535 --> 00:13:35,400
I've been living here
for about a year now

162
00:13:35,435 --> 00:13:39,094
and I will
warn you, it is quiet.

163
00:13:39,128 --> 00:13:43,029
There's really like
nothing to do at all.

164
00:13:43,063 --> 00:13:44,133
The closest bar

165
00:13:44,168 --> 00:13:46,273
that doesn't have
a bowling alley attached to it

166
00:13:46,308 --> 00:13:48,172
is actually all the way up
in Buffalo.

167
00:13:48,206 --> 00:13:53,625
Um, I don't drive
or bowl, but it's all good.

168
00:13:53,660 --> 00:13:55,420
Mhm. Mhm.
Want one?

169
00:13:55,455 --> 00:13:56,663
- Oh, no. Thanks.
- I have more

170
00:13:56,697 --> 00:13:58,941
I'm good. I know, thank you.
They look delicious though.

171
00:13:58,976 --> 00:14:00,046
- Yeah.
- Crispy.

172
00:14:00,080 --> 00:14:03,946
I've been having migraines
sort of general all over

173
00:14:03,981 --> 00:14:08,261
aches and pains like every
joint is on fire.

174
00:14:09,469 --> 00:14:11,678
But they got
a pill for that.

175
00:14:11,712 --> 00:14:13,473
They got a pill for everything.
A pill for this,

176
00:14:13,507 --> 00:14:15,475
a pill for that.
Pill for the fucking pills.

177
00:14:17,097 --> 00:14:19,134
I actually moved here

178
00:14:19,168 --> 00:14:22,102
because I was going to take
some college classes.

179
00:14:22,137 --> 00:14:23,690
You know, Genesee College.
- Yeah, yeah.

180
00:14:23,724 --> 00:14:24,898
- Just up.
- Yeah.

181
00:14:24,933 --> 00:14:25,968
Poetry.

182
00:14:26,003 --> 00:14:27,176
Oh.

183
00:14:27,211 --> 00:14:30,283
I did get involved
with the... teacher.

184
00:14:31,456 --> 00:14:32,872
Grace, whose...

185
00:14:34,287 --> 00:14:38,222
a bitch and dumped me
out of a blue.

186
00:14:41,294 --> 00:14:42,640
And just kind of...

187
00:14:43,537 --> 00:14:46,540
You feel used, you know,

188
00:14:46,575 --> 00:14:50,959
you just want back
everything they took from you.

189
00:14:52,546 --> 00:14:54,169
I'm trying to track her down.

190
00:14:54,514 --> 00:14:55,929
I'll find her.

191
00:14:58,173 --> 00:14:59,346
Is that your husband?

192
00:15:00,140 --> 00:15:03,592
Oh, no.
That's, uh, my cousin Winthrop.

193
00:15:04,282 --> 00:15:05,249
Hmm.

194
00:15:07,182 --> 00:15:08,424
You need a hand?

195
00:15:08,459 --> 00:15:10,116
I've killed a few weeds
in my day.

196
00:15:10,150 --> 00:15:11,669
Honestly. No, you
don't need to.

197
00:15:11,703 --> 00:15:12,946
- You sure?
- Yeah. No, I--

198
00:15:12,981 --> 00:15:14,292
Your ice cream is
probably melted.

199
00:15:14,327 --> 00:15:15,397
No. That's fine.

200
00:15:15,431 --> 00:15:17,295
I can just put it
in your fridge.

201
00:15:18,365 --> 00:15:19,435
Um...

202
00:15:20,781 --> 00:15:22,300
- Oh. Ellen. Ellen.
- Ellen.

203
00:15:22,335 --> 00:15:23,612
Yeah. Uh.
Let me, uh...

204
00:15:23,646 --> 00:15:24,647
Okay. Here.

205
00:15:24,682 --> 00:15:25,476
You can get the other bag.

206
00:15:25,510 --> 00:15:27,685
I will.
I'm just going to show you

207
00:15:27,719 --> 00:15:29,514
where the kitchen
is first and then.

208
00:15:29,549 --> 00:15:30,481
Hi.

209
00:15:31,344 --> 00:15:32,345
Hi.

210
00:15:55,437 --> 00:15:58,060
Who watches TV on
such a beautiful day.

211
00:15:59,337 --> 00:16:00,683
It's a good day for gardening.

212
00:16:00,718 --> 00:16:01,684
Let's do it.

213
00:16:01,719 --> 00:16:03,169
Mm.

214
00:16:05,136 --> 00:16:08,381
It's so nice to have
somebody to actually talk to.

215
00:16:11,453 --> 00:16:12,626
Here are some gloves.

216
00:16:12,661 --> 00:16:14,318
How long ago did
your mother pass?

217
00:16:17,390 --> 00:16:18,736
I saw the photos.

218
00:16:21,601 --> 00:16:22,705
Just a few months back.

219
00:16:22,740 --> 00:16:23,741
Mm.

220
00:16:23,775 --> 00:16:25,122
She was pretty.

221
00:16:35,235 --> 00:16:36,236
Doesn't that hurt?

222
00:16:38,169 --> 00:16:39,412
Oh, Ellen...

223
00:16:42,139 --> 00:16:43,795
Everything hurts.

224
00:16:52,701 --> 00:16:53,564
Mm.

225
00:17:00,778 --> 00:17:02,262
Almost there?

226
00:17:02,297 --> 00:17:03,229
Mm.

227
00:17:14,102 --> 00:17:15,068
Sorry.

228
00:17:17,277 --> 00:17:18,520
Oh. It slipped.

229
00:17:20,763 --> 00:17:22,351
All right, here we go.

230
00:17:24,629 --> 00:17:27,149
Winthrop, dinner
if you're hungry.

231
00:17:34,191 --> 00:17:35,640
You must be Winthrop.

232
00:17:37,297 --> 00:17:39,541
Winthrop, Vahna,

233
00:17:39,575 --> 00:17:41,163
our neighbor who was
kind enough

234
00:17:41,198 --> 00:17:42,785
to provide us
with this beautiful food.

235
00:17:57,593 --> 00:18:01,321
So what's a guy like you
doing living with his cousin?

236
00:18:01,356 --> 00:18:03,599
Don't you have a job?

237
00:18:06,671 --> 00:18:08,190
He lined up a job
for the spring.

238
00:18:09,295 --> 00:18:10,675
Not too far away, actually.

239
00:18:10,710 --> 00:18:11,642
Oh, yeah.

240
00:18:12,781 --> 00:18:13,851
What kind of job?

241
00:18:17,510 --> 00:18:18,683
Sheet metal plant.

242
00:18:21,617 --> 00:18:23,102
Does he speak?

243
00:18:29,280 --> 00:18:30,557
I speak.

244
00:18:31,834 --> 00:18:34,527
Sorry, I was just teasing.
I didn't mean anything.

245
00:18:39,394 --> 00:18:42,293
Okay. Get home safely.

246
00:18:42,328 --> 00:18:43,605
Yeah.

247
00:18:43,639 --> 00:18:45,745
How long has Winthrop
been staying with you?

248
00:18:47,264 --> 00:18:48,265
Not long.

249
00:18:48,644 --> 00:18:50,612
Just be careful.

250
00:18:52,303 --> 00:18:55,341
I can tell that man has
done some terrible things.

251
00:19:00,380 --> 00:19:01,692
- Okay.
- Mm.

252
00:19:09,286 --> 00:19:10,287
Toodles.

253
00:19:28,650 --> 00:19:30,721
<i>I'm sorry, I didn't know
you were in there.</i>

254
00:19:31,411 --> 00:19:32,964
<i>It won't happen again.</i>

255
00:19:37,659 --> 00:19:41,214
You think you can hide from me?

256
00:19:43,251 --> 00:19:44,735
Anywhere you go...

257
00:19:44,769 --> 00:19:46,944
I will find you.

258
00:19:47,531 --> 00:19:49,878
Bitch! Bitch! Bitch!

259
00:19:49,912 --> 00:19:51,362
Bitch!

260
00:20:13,073 --> 00:20:14,454
Thank you.

261
00:20:16,594 --> 00:20:18,907
I wanted to apologize
again about last night.

262
00:20:20,460 --> 00:20:21,496
It's okay.

263
00:20:33,749 --> 00:20:34,992
The kitchen accident.

264
00:20:37,097 --> 00:20:38,409
In the mess hall.

265
00:20:40,584 --> 00:20:42,620
Had these huge vats of fry oil.

266
00:20:44,864 --> 00:20:47,729
Some guys were messing around.

267
00:20:48,730 --> 00:20:50,041
One of them tipped.

268
00:20:53,321 --> 00:20:54,494
Almost killed me.

269
00:20:54,770 --> 00:20:55,978
Probably should have.

270
00:21:08,991 --> 00:21:10,579
You fixed it.

271
00:21:10,614 --> 00:21:11,684
It's really beautiful.

272
00:21:23,351 --> 00:21:24,455
Thank you.

273
00:21:32,152 --> 00:21:34,741
We should have taken you in
when your parents died.

274
00:21:35,949 --> 00:21:37,399
I'm so sorry.

275
00:21:45,787 --> 00:21:46,891
Vahna.

276
00:21:46,926 --> 00:21:47,858
Hi.

277
00:21:49,031 --> 00:21:50,412
Hide the silverware.

278
00:21:51,896 --> 00:21:54,105
I heard about your
church fundraiser,

279
00:21:54,140 --> 00:21:55,624
so I brought this stuff.

280
00:21:55,659 --> 00:21:57,868
It's not a lot,
but I don't use it anymore.

281
00:21:57,902 --> 00:21:59,110
That's so generous.

282
00:21:59,145 --> 00:22:00,111
Yeah. And then I was...

283
00:22:00,146 --> 00:22:02,942
Well, I was just
sitting around bored sick

284
00:22:02,976 --> 00:22:06,566
and I thought maybe my new
friend Ellen wouldn't mind

285
00:22:06,601 --> 00:22:09,155
keeping her silly little
friend company for a while.

286
00:22:09,189 --> 00:22:11,364
Well, we're pretty
much done for the day.

287
00:22:11,399 --> 00:22:12,641
The sky's about to open up.

288
00:22:12,676 --> 00:22:14,678
Oh, well, look at that.
Yeah, okay.

289
00:22:25,516 --> 00:22:26,310
Good times.

290
00:22:26,345 --> 00:22:28,726
- Yeah.
- Good times and hard times.

291
00:22:30,728 --> 00:22:31,936
Oh, no.

292
00:22:33,041 --> 00:22:35,630
I know all about hard times.

293
00:22:35,664 --> 00:22:37,873
The cruelty people
are capable of.

294
00:22:38,702 --> 00:22:39,944
Like my father.

295
00:22:41,567 --> 00:22:43,603
He knew cruelty.

296
00:22:44,501 --> 00:22:46,537
He was an expert.

297
00:22:46,951 --> 00:22:50,610
Not only did he start to
sexually assault his daughter,

298
00:22:50,645 --> 00:22:52,854
when I was, like,
four years old.

299
00:22:53,613 --> 00:22:55,097
He thought it would be fun

300
00:22:55,132 --> 00:22:58,100
to pass her around to all
of his friends.

301
00:22:59,619 --> 00:23:02,035
All of them like
a cheap bottle of wine.

302
00:23:04,210 --> 00:23:05,798
Do you know what that's like?

303
00:23:06,592 --> 00:23:09,491
While your father sits back
and it's just like, you know,

304
00:23:09,526 --> 00:23:11,976
"Let it feel good.
Like, why are you crying?"

305
00:23:16,256 --> 00:23:17,430
No.

306
00:23:18,224 --> 00:23:19,398
I don't.

307
00:23:20,675 --> 00:23:21,986
And I see how strong you are.

308
00:23:23,229 --> 00:23:25,093
Survivors carry it
in their eyes.

309
00:23:27,164 --> 00:23:28,510
Strong.

310
00:23:28,786 --> 00:23:29,856
Yeah.

311
00:23:30,788 --> 00:23:31,893
No.

312
00:23:34,758 --> 00:23:38,900
I would die right now
if I had a choice.

313
00:23:41,489 --> 00:23:43,594
I just need a new fucking body.

314
00:23:47,909 --> 00:23:50,049
Every inch of this one hurts.

315
00:23:51,015 --> 00:23:54,502
I put the bird bath into
the shed so the paint won't run.

316
00:24:00,680 --> 00:24:02,648
I think I'm gonna rest
for a while.

317
00:24:02,682 --> 00:24:03,683
Tired?

318
00:24:04,822 --> 00:24:07,204
From all that yard work?

319
00:24:08,308 --> 00:24:10,138
Big, strong guy like you.

320
00:24:12,692 --> 00:24:14,211
What do you want from me?

321
00:24:16,075 --> 00:24:17,697
Everything.

322
00:24:18,905 --> 00:24:21,770
Ignore her, Winthrop.
She's being silly.

323
00:24:21,805 --> 00:24:23,807
Yes, ignore me.
I'm being silly.

324
00:24:30,089 --> 00:24:31,573
You can't trust him.

325
00:24:31,608 --> 00:24:33,230
Stop. You don't know him.

326
00:24:35,715 --> 00:24:37,821
He wants to fuck me
and probably you too.

327
00:24:39,167 --> 00:24:40,686
Probably you too.

328
00:24:40,720 --> 00:24:42,757
Don't be so naive.

329
00:24:42,791 --> 00:24:43,861
Can you dance with me?

330
00:24:43,896 --> 00:24:45,829
- I'm good, I'm good.
- Oh, please dance with me,

331
00:24:45,863 --> 00:24:46,899
- I won't bite.
- Really.

332
00:24:46,933 --> 00:24:48,521
I don't bite, I promise.

333
00:24:54,769 --> 00:24:58,945
You put up a very
puritan front, Ellen.

334
00:24:58,980 --> 00:25:02,915
But I think you got
some secrets in there.

335
00:25:03,743 --> 00:25:05,020
I don't have any secrets.

336
00:25:05,055 --> 00:25:05,987
No?

337
00:25:09,715 --> 00:25:10,785
It's getting late.

338
00:25:11,095 --> 00:25:12,856
I'm tired.
Let's get you home.

339
00:25:12,890 --> 00:25:15,099
I had to drink a lot of wine, actually.

340
00:25:15,790 --> 00:25:18,240
A lot of wine,
and it's raining outside.

341
00:25:18,275 --> 00:25:21,243
And I don't want to crash
my bike into a ditch.

342
00:25:21,278 --> 00:25:22,900
Okay. Uh, I will drive you.

343
00:25:22,935 --> 00:25:24,177
We'll put your bike
in the back.

344
00:25:24,212 --> 00:25:26,007
