792
01:07:36,466 --> 01:07:40,849
This man told Vahna she no
longer had to be afraid

793
01:07:40,884 --> 01:07:42,679
that she would now live forever.

794
01:07:42,713 --> 01:07:44,715
[sinister voice
I got something for you.

795
01:07:45,337 --> 01:07:46,786
And you get to keep it.

796
01:07:52,240 --> 01:07:55,588
And Vahna swore to me
that if I ever left her,

797
01:07:55,623 --> 01:07:58,453
she would do whatever it took
to find me.

798
01:08:01,146 --> 01:08:04,183
I'm, um, changing my number, so.

799
01:08:04,218 --> 01:08:06,427
Wait...
I found some letters.

800
01:08:07,221 --> 01:08:09,119
Some are to you.

801
01:08:09,602 --> 01:08:11,328
I just thought if we could meet.

802
01:08:11,363 --> 01:08:12,295
You saw the letters,

803
01:08:12,329 --> 01:08:13,882
maybe we could make
some sense of this.

804
01:08:16,161 --> 01:08:17,300
Grace.

805
01:08:20,889 --> 01:08:22,098
Grace...

806
01:08:23,789 --> 01:08:25,756
Vahna's not dead.

807
01:08:25,791 --> 01:08:27,551
What do you mean?

808
01:08:27,586 --> 01:08:28,518
Move.

809
01:08:28,794 --> 01:08:30,485
And leave no trace.

810
01:08:31,210 --> 01:08:33,316
Vahna is not dead.

811
01:09:17,256 --> 01:09:18,257
Help!

812
01:09:18,499 --> 01:09:19,810
Help!

813
01:09:25,816 --> 01:09:28,233
Where's Grace Beck?!

814
01:09:28,819 --> 01:09:31,477
Where is Grace Beck?!

815
01:09:35,309 --> 01:09:36,413
Kevin.

816
01:09:38,795 --> 01:09:40,521
What the fuck is going on?

817
01:09:40,555 --> 01:09:41,591
Drop it!

818
01:09:42,730 --> 01:09:43,972
Drop it!

819
01:09:46,043 --> 01:09:47,528
Who are you?

820
01:09:47,735 --> 01:09:48,943
Got him.

821
01:09:54,328 --> 01:09:55,674
Let's get him outta here.

822
01:09:56,019 --> 01:09:57,400
Did he hurt you?

823
01:09:57,641 --> 01:09:58,470
James.

824
01:10:08,618 --> 01:10:09,619
Hey!

825
01:12:14,019 --> 01:12:16,504
What are you doing
with Winthrop?

826
01:12:16,539 --> 01:12:17,885
It's freezing out here.

827
01:12:17,919 --> 01:12:19,852
Come inside where we can talk.

828
01:12:22,683 --> 01:12:26,065
My name is James,
and this is Kevin.

829
01:12:30,622 --> 01:12:31,933
We'll be inside.

830
01:12:57,234 --> 01:13:00,479
Hi, my name is James Light

831
01:13:00,514 --> 01:13:03,482
and I'm a priest
like Father Caldwell.

832
01:13:05,933 --> 01:13:08,107
And this is Doctor Emily Warren.

833
01:13:08,142 --> 01:13:09,592
Hello, Ellen.

834
01:13:09,626 --> 01:13:10,765
How's Winthrop doing?

835
01:13:10,800 --> 01:13:11,939
Sleeping peacefully.

836
01:13:11,973 --> 01:13:13,216
I'd like to see him.

837
01:13:13,250 --> 01:13:15,770
It will take some time for the
tranquilizers to wear off,

838
01:13:15,805 --> 01:13:17,945
but I can assure you
he's safe.

839
01:13:17,979 --> 01:13:19,843
Here, why don't you have
a seat

840
01:13:19,878 --> 01:13:20,982
and we'll tell you everything.

841
01:13:29,957 --> 01:13:35,790
We're dealing with nothing less
than evil incarnate.

842
01:13:35,825 --> 01:13:38,034
Some people call them demons.

843
01:13:39,000 --> 01:13:42,590
Imps. Succubi. Djinni.

844
01:13:42,625 --> 01:13:46,111
They like to nestle in and hide,

845
01:13:46,939 --> 01:13:49,528
forcing us to seek them out.

846
01:13:49,563 --> 01:13:53,532
One of these entities
had been in Vahna Minter

847
01:13:53,567 --> 01:13:55,431
for a very long time,

848
01:13:56,570 --> 01:14:00,159
and is now residing in Winthrop.

849
01:14:02,023 --> 01:14:04,854
Vahna was taken very young.

850
01:14:05,510 --> 01:14:10,791
The evil infusing in her
its own twisted desires,

851
01:14:11,205 --> 01:14:13,759
becoming obsessed
with Grace Beck.

852
01:14:14,173 --> 01:14:17,867
But Grace had enough
self-worth to get away in time.

853
01:14:17,901 --> 01:14:20,525
And this is when
we lost track of Vahna.

854
01:14:20,559 --> 01:14:21,560
Which is too bad

855
01:14:21,595 --> 01:14:24,114
because I believe
we could have captured it

856
01:14:24,149 --> 01:14:25,530
and saved her life.

857
01:14:26,116 --> 01:14:27,255
How?

858
01:14:27,290 --> 01:14:31,087
Evil is seeking those
who've been weakened by abuse,

859
01:14:31,121 --> 01:14:35,194
neglect, drugs like
Vahna Minter or Winthrop.

860
01:14:35,229 --> 01:14:39,095
The abuse rewires pathways,
making the brain

861
01:14:39,129 --> 01:14:42,029
more vulnerable, allowing
possession to take hold.

862
01:14:42,063 --> 01:14:48,276
But in very rare cases, a brain
is forming a neural cage

863
01:14:48,311 --> 01:14:50,209
that an entity cannot escape.

864
01:14:51,107 --> 01:14:52,591
You lost me here.

865
01:14:52,971 --> 01:14:54,869
We have such a brain.

866
01:14:55,145 --> 01:14:56,630
Kevin, do you mind?

867
01:15:02,567 --> 01:15:04,845
The book tells us about them.

868
01:15:06,156 --> 01:15:10,057
Now, the language used
is very archaic,

869
01:15:10,091 --> 01:15:13,785
but it translates
something akin to lockbox.

870
01:15:15,303 --> 01:15:19,100
Now, the only way to save
Winthrop now is

871
01:15:19,135 --> 01:15:22,310
to have the very
powerful force inside him

872
01:15:22,345 --> 01:15:27,005
moved into another host,
one that he can't escape.

873
01:15:27,039 --> 01:15:28,075
A lockbox.

874
01:15:28,109 --> 01:15:31,975
Surely you sense something
strange in Winthrop.

875
01:15:32,286 --> 01:15:33,839
A change.

876
01:15:34,391 --> 01:15:35,565
Yes.

877
01:15:36,186 --> 01:15:37,947
He told me he felt like

878
01:15:37,981 --> 01:15:40,087
he was thinking someone
else's thoughts.

879
01:15:44,712 --> 01:15:45,989
Here it comes.

880
01:15:59,244 --> 01:16:00,866
What are you doing
with that boy?

881
01:16:00,901 --> 01:16:02,730
James, we need
to get him upstairs.

882
01:16:03,420 --> 01:16:08,149
That boy was in a coma at
Saint Mary's for almost a year.

883
01:16:08,356 --> 01:16:12,395
His brain scan shows
he has the neural cage.

884
01:16:12,429 --> 01:16:13,672
What?

885
01:16:13,707 --> 01:16:14,984
So he was sent to us,

886
01:16:15,950 --> 01:16:17,952
and he just might save Winthrop.

887
01:16:17,987 --> 01:16:19,851
Are you fucking kidding me?

888
01:16:19,885 --> 01:16:21,231
He's the lock box?

889
01:16:21,715 --> 01:16:23,924
He's more than a child.

890
01:16:23,958 --> 01:16:28,998
He has the ability to absorb
pain like water into sand.

891
01:16:29,274 --> 01:16:32,760
The boy was born to parents
whose cruelty

892
01:16:32,795 --> 01:16:34,935
was matched only
by their neglect.

893
01:16:35,694 --> 01:16:37,800
They drugged him.

894
01:16:37,834 --> 01:16:39,249
They abandoned him.

895
01:16:39,284 --> 01:16:42,149
So now we do our best
to take care of him.

896
01:16:42,701 --> 01:16:44,772
But he was built for this.

897
01:17:16,873 --> 01:17:19,117
Yeah. Brave boy.

898
01:17:19,151 --> 01:17:20,083
Mm.

899
01:17:20,946 --> 01:17:23,362
We should be good
to go by sunset.

900
01:17:44,521 --> 01:17:46,420
Do you have a nosebleed?

901
01:17:46,454 --> 01:17:47,386
Mmhmm.

902
01:17:47,904 --> 01:17:48,733
Here.

903
01:17:50,873 --> 01:17:51,874
I got it.

904
01:18:07,199 --> 01:18:09,270
Feed us now.

905
01:18:12,377 --> 01:18:14,034
Why are you here?

906
01:18:15,863 --> 01:18:17,244
You vile...

907
01:18:17,278 --> 01:18:19,280
obscene creatures.

908
01:18:21,213 --> 01:18:22,870
We are you.

909
01:18:25,321 --> 01:18:26,943
And if you let them do this,

910
01:18:26,978 --> 01:18:28,980
Winthrop will die.

911
01:18:49,586 --> 01:18:50,760
James.

912
01:18:52,555 --> 01:18:55,972
Those things in that boy

913
01:18:57,560 --> 01:19:01,081
just told me that if you
do this, Winthrop will die.

914
01:19:01,115 --> 01:19:03,048
They spoke to you?

915
01:19:03,083 --> 01:19:04,015
Yeah.

916
01:19:05,844 --> 01:19:08,122
They are the prince of lies.

917
01:19:08,157 --> 01:19:10,262
He does not stand in the truth

918
01:19:10,297 --> 01:19:13,058
because there
is no truth in him.

919
01:19:13,093 --> 01:19:14,439
So no one has ever died.

920
01:19:16,890 --> 01:19:20,790
There is always a chance
that something goes wrong.

921
01:19:22,619 --> 01:19:24,104
How many have you lost?

922
01:19:26,934 --> 01:19:28,039
Two.

923
01:19:28,073 --> 01:19:29,247
Out of how many?

924
01:19:30,869 --> 01:19:31,870
Eight.

925
01:19:34,459 --> 01:19:37,048
The evil that is in Winthrop,

926
01:19:37,082 --> 01:19:39,982
do you know how many
lives it has destroyed?

927
01:19:40,016 --> 01:19:41,604
Condemning their souls to hell.

928
01:19:41,638 --> 01:19:42,847
So this is a bargain?

929
01:19:42,881 --> 01:19:43,917
No.

930
01:19:43,951 --> 01:19:45,332
It is God's work.

931
01:19:45,366 --> 01:19:48,300
God doesn't trade souls.
That is the devil's work.

932
01:19:48,335 --> 01:19:51,925
Morgan Hetfield,
a mother of five.

933
01:19:51,959 --> 01:19:53,443
Brandon Paige, a surgeon

934
01:19:53,478 --> 01:19:55,445
who has since saved
hundreds of lives.

935
01:19:55,480 --> 01:19:57,482
These are just two
of the people

936
01:19:57,516 --> 01:19:59,518
this remarkable boy
has saved.

937
01:20:03,350 --> 01:20:04,351
All right,

938
01:20:05,214 --> 01:20:06,491
I'll tell you what.

939
01:20:07,526 --> 01:20:10,184
If you believe what we're doing
is wrong,

940
01:20:10,219 --> 01:20:12,911
then take Winthrop
and walk out that door.

941
01:20:12,946 --> 01:20:14,154
We won't stop you.

942
01:20:19,366 --> 01:20:22,300
Winthrop is not dying tonight.

943
01:20:22,990 --> 01:20:24,440
Do you understand that?

944
01:21:08,104 --> 01:21:09,312
Now, now.

945
01:21:13,696 --> 01:21:16,216
Don't go losing your head.

946
01:21:22,429 --> 01:21:23,430
Who are you?

947
01:21:27,710 --> 01:21:29,919
That's who I am.

948
01:21:29,954 --> 01:21:31,576
Not to sound like your uncle.

949
01:21:32,094 --> 01:21:34,337
I'm not done with you.

950
01:21:40,033 --> 01:21:41,103
Argh!

951
01:21:48,317 --> 01:21:50,629
I've got something for you.

952
01:21:52,597 --> 01:21:54,150
And you.

953
01:21:54,426 --> 01:21:55,565
Get.

954
01:21:56,325 --> 01:21:57,982
To keep it.

955
01:24:29,271 --> 01:24:31,583
Sorry. We should have
known better, I'm sorry.

956
01:24:32,308 --> 01:24:33,861
All right.
We'll take him down now.

957
01:24:33,896 --> 01:24:36,312
All right, let's get you up,
Winthrop.

958
01:24:36,726 --> 01:24:37,658
Okay.

959
01:24:45,942 --> 01:24:47,806
Let's take him
to the basement.

960
01:25:31,850 --> 01:25:33,749
What do we do now?

961
01:25:34,370 --> 01:25:35,682
We wait.

962
01:26:14,721 --> 01:26:15,825
Is that normal?

963
01:26:16,412 --> 01:26:17,689
It's fine.

964
01:26:20,796 --> 01:26:22,349
Help me!

965
01:26:25,801 --> 01:26:26,905
Help!

966
01:26:34,499 --> 01:26:35,604
What?

967
01:26:37,330 --> 01:26:38,538
What just happened?

968
01:26:40,747 --> 01:26:42,266
What's going on?

969
01:26:42,300 --> 01:26:43,508
The video always cuts out.

970
01:26:43,543 --> 01:26:45,890
We're not allowed to see what
happens in the transition.

971
01:26:45,924 --> 01:26:47,305
Ellen!

972
01:26:49,859 --> 01:26:51,620
Ellen! Help!

973
01:26:53,656 --> 01:26:54,726
Help

974
01:26:56,832 --> 01:26:58,005
What?

975
01:26:59,938 --> 01:27:00,939
James?

976
01:27:15,471 --> 01:27:16,955
James. We're losing him.

977
01:27:26,620 --> 01:27:27,759
Ellen?

978
01:27:27,794 --> 01:27:28,795
Ellen!

979
01:27:56,340 --> 01:27:57,341
Oh.

980
01:27:57,651 --> 01:27:59,274
No!

981
01:28:02,035 --> 01:28:03,795
No!

982
01:28:15,531 --> 01:28:16,567
Ugh!

983
01:30:05,054 --> 01:30:06,055
Mom.

984
01:30:27,836 --> 01:30:28,871
My...

985
01:30:29,907 --> 01:30:30,908
Ellen.

986
01:30:31,702 --> 01:30:33,082
You're not her.

987
01:30:33,980 --> 01:30:35,982
Don't you dare use her voice.

988
01:30:38,709 --> 01:30:40,055
I'm Winthrop.

989
01:30:41,608 --> 01:30:44,542
You knew where he was going.

990
01:30:45,578 --> 01:30:49,789
To that sick sadistic uncle

991
01:30:49,823 --> 01:30:54,621
who would beat him
until he could no longer cry.

992
01:30:54,656 --> 01:30:55,588
No.

993
01:30:57,244 --> 01:30:58,970
I didn't know.

994
01:30:59,005 --> 01:31:00,627
Don't lie to me again.

995
01:31:03,665 --> 01:31:05,252
You did know.

996
01:31:07,082 --> 01:31:08,083
Yes.

997
01:31:12,708 --> 01:31:14,123
I know who I owe.

998
01:31:17,920 --> 01:31:19,197
And you're not him.

999
01:31:40,771 --> 01:31:41,772
Hello.

1000
01:31:47,363 --> 01:31:48,537
Hi.

1001
01:31:49,193 --> 01:31:50,263
I've got to go.

1002
01:31:54,681 --> 01:31:55,820
Do you have a name?

1003
01:31:56,338 --> 01:31:59,652
I used to, but I don't remember.

1004
01:32:02,724 --> 01:32:04,519
Thank you for saving Winthrop.

1005
01:32:13,320 --> 01:32:15,046
You can walk?

1006
01:32:16,876 --> 01:32:18,187
Yes.

1007
01:32:53,119 --> 01:32:54,569
Ellen?

1008
01:33:00,367 --> 01:33:01,368
Where is it?

1009
01:33:02,715 --> 01:33:04,924
No more games.

1010
01:33:12,172 --> 01:33:14,347
Open the door!!!

1011
01:33:17,419 --> 01:33:18,593
Ellen.

1012
01:33:20,905 --> 01:33:23,045
You interrupted us.
I don't have it.

1013
01:33:23,080 --> 01:33:25,047
Ellen! We're coming in!

1014
01:33:26,014 --> 01:33:27,705
Open the door!

1015
01:33:27,740 --> 01:33:28,844
I can still finish this.

1016
01:33:28,879 --> 01:33:29,880
He's lying.

1017
01:33:29,914 --> 01:33:30,950
Open the door!

1018
01:33:30,984 --> 01:33:31,916
Ellen!

1019
01:33:47,414 --> 01:33:48,519
God,

1020
01:33:49,485 --> 01:33:53,386
give me counsel, for I am
facing the Prince of Lies.

1021
01:33:53,420 --> 01:33:57,459
Give me the wisdom to not fall
for his wicked tricks,

1022
01:33:57,493 --> 01:34:00,773
for it is but deception
that gives him his power.

1023
01:34:00,807 --> 01:34:02,671
It is the Prince of Lies.

1024
01:34:02,706 --> 01:34:04,777
God, give me counsel.

1025
01:34:05,432 --> 01:34:07,262
...For facing the Prince
of Lies.

1026
01:34:09,471 --> 01:34:10,921
What is it, then?

1027
01:34:12,163 --> 01:34:13,164
What's the lie?

1028
01:34:19,861 --> 01:34:21,138
It's in me.

1029
01:34:25,936 --> 01:34:26,937
Ellen!

1030
01:34:30,872 --> 01:34:32,149
Touch my hand!

1031
01:34:32,183 --> 01:34:36,947
You will not touch the boy!

1032
01:35:41,597 --> 01:35:44,083
He's got it.
It's um...

1033
01:35:44,117 --> 01:35:45,118
Okay.

1034
01:35:45,532 --> 01:35:46,533
Okay.

1035
01:36:07,554 --> 01:36:09,142
What happened down there?

1036
01:36:11,904 --> 01:36:13,250
It tried to pull me apart.

1037
01:36:15,908 --> 01:36:16,943
Didn't work.

1038
01:36:20,015 --> 01:36:21,361
Someone brought you up, right?

1039
01:36:24,295 --> 01:36:25,296
Yeah.

1040
01:36:27,126 --> 01:36:28,817
The boy is resting now.

1041
01:36:29,162 --> 01:36:30,577
- I'll pay him a visit.
- Okay.

1042
01:36:32,614 --> 01:36:36,135
If we give you a tape recorder
would you be willing

1043
01:36:36,169 --> 01:36:40,380
to share what happened on record
just for us

1044
01:36:40,415 --> 01:36:42,175
for the next time we
try to save someone?

1045
01:36:43,521 --> 01:36:44,522
Sure.

1046
01:36:45,178 --> 01:36:46,179
Okay.

1047
01:36:48,147 --> 01:36:49,251
Thank you, James.

1048
01:36:50,045 --> 01:36:51,357
Oh, yes.

1049
01:36:52,116 --> 01:36:53,393
You're welcome.

1050
01:37:22,422 --> 01:37:26,185
That thing was destroying
the last good memory I had.

1051
01:37:29,291 --> 01:37:31,052
But you wouldn't let it.

1052
01:37:39,232 --> 01:37:40,889
Thank you.

1053
01:37:43,961 --> 01:37:45,652
Let's not make a thing of it.

1054
01:38:12,403 --> 01:38:14,233
<i>Dear cousin Ellen.</i>

1055
01:38:14,267 --> 01:38:16,442
<i>I saw this Michael
the Archangel</i>

1056
01:38:16,476 --> 01:38:19,479
<i>vanquishing the demon, and
it reminded me of you.</i>

1057
01:38:21,205 --> 01:38:23,587
<i>I wanted to let you know
I started my new job</i>

1058
01:38:23,621 --> 01:38:25,485
<i>and I really like it so far.</i>

1059
01:38:26,176 --> 01:38:27,591
<i>Maybe you want to come?</i>

1060
01:38:28,178 --> 01:38:29,627
<i>See the new place?</i>

1061
01:38:30,421 --> 01:38:32,113
<i>It would be good to see you.</i>

1062
01:38:33,390 --> 01:38:35,288
<i>Love, Winthrop.</i>